      <p class="lead">In an era where fast food combo meals routinely eclipse the $12 mark, Dairy Queen stands out as an intriguing economic anomaly. Between the legendary 4-course $7 Meal Deal and the customizable 2-for-$5 Mix &amp; Match platform, the chain maintains price points that feel straight out of 2018. But are these deals genuine steals, or do hidden upcharges and diminished portion sizes erode your savings? <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu Research Desk</a> conducted a line-item receipt audit across regional franchise locations to reveal the true mathematical efficiency of DQ’s value menu.</p>

      <h2>Receipt Forensics: Auditing the $7 Meal Deal</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">Dairy Queen $7 Meal Deal</a> is a multi-tier bundle consisting of an entrée, side of regular fries, a 21-ounce fountain beverage, and a small sundae. To assess real savings, we audited the individual à la carte retail prices of each component across 15 standard US franchise markets:</p>

